      en: ["Longest and historically most significant river valley in Belize.", "Fertile corridor for agriculture and cattle ranching.", "Former 'highway' for mahogany transport in the 18th and 19th centuries.", "Houses a variety of Maya ruins and historical settlements.", "Characterized by rich alluvial soils and seasonal flooding.", "Central habitat for the endangered Central American River Turtle.", "Connects the Cayo and Belize districts over a length of 200 km.", "Important corridor for national travel and goods traffic."]
